{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>In this wilderness your carcasses shall fall.</b> It appears that in this sin Israel were in three groups: some wept, some complained against Mosheh and against Aharon and said 'we are dying,' and some said 'let us set a leader.' Corresponding to them Scripture mentions 'your carcasses' three times. And it used the expression 'your carcasses' so that you not understand in this the destruction of the souls — rather only the carcasses died, and they have a share in the World to Come. And this is what it says at the end of its words: 'in this wilderness they shall be completed' — that is, the carcasses, not the souls. 'And all your numbered ones, according to all your count, from twenty years old and upward' — the tribe of Levi was not included in this, for their count was from one month old and upward."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:28.667999940Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}